# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and deployed to
# Linux, which is the exact combination that produces
#
#   bash: $'\r': command not found
#
# on the server. Git normalises on clone, so `git clone` on the VM would
# be fine - but copying a file straight across with scp would not, and
# that is a failure with no obvious cause and no obvious fix.
#
# Pinning eol=lf means these files are LF in the working tree on every
# platform, so both routes work.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf

# Video is binary; without this, autocrlf would corrupt it on checkout.
*.mp4       binary
*.mov       binary
*.webm      binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
